    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for the E.164 telephone in `E164Telephone.toE164()`:\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/E164Telephone.java`**\n- After the existing general 8\u201315 total-digit check, the national-number length is now validated against the country code:\n  - `+61` \u2192 national number must be exactly **9** digits (total 11 after `+`)\n  - `+1` \u2192 national number must be exactly **10** digits (total 11 after `+`)\n  - Other country codes remain bound only by the general 8\u201315 total-digit rule.\n- A wrong length throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the existing `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` already maps to **400**.\n- Updated the class Javadoc to document the new rule.\n\nThis flows through the existing `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` step in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, so `\"+61 123\"` (only 3 national digits) is rejected with 400.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The valid-path payloads are unaffected: `uniqueTelephone()` normalizes to `+61` + 9 national digits, satisfying the new rule.",
